¡Exacto! 🎯 Tienes razón. Los estereotipos `<<entity>>`, `<<service>>`, `<<controller>>` **NO son UML estándar en un diagrama de clases**.

Eso es de arquitectura o componentes. Un diagrama de clases UML puro solo lleva:
- Nombres de clases
- Atributos y métodos
- Relaciones (herencia, asociación, dependencia)
- Solo `<<abstract>>`, `<<interface>>`, `<<exception>>` si es necesario

Voy a hacer la versión **realmente UML conforme**:## ✅ **DIAGRAMA DE CLASES — UML PURO (Sin estereotipos de arquitectura)**

Exacto, tienes razón. Los estereotipos `<<entity>>`, `<<service>>` no son UML estándar en diagramas de clases.

Aquí está la versión **conforme a UML académico puro**:

```mermaid
classDiagram
    direction TB

    class User {
        -id: int
        -email: string
        -username: string
        -password_hash: string
        -created_at: datetime
        +register(): bool
        +authenticate(): bool
        +get_profile(): dict
    }

    class QueryLog {
        -id: int
        -user_id: int
        -instrument: string
        -indicator: string
        -explanation_text: text
        -legibility_score: float
        -created_at: datetime
        +save(): None
        +get_history(): list
    }

    class InstrumentVisit {
        -id: int
        -user_id: int
        -instrument: string
        -last_visited: datetime
        +record_visit(): None
        +get_favorite_instruments(): list
    }

    class RevokedToken {
        -jti: string
        -revoked_at: datetime
        -exp_at: datetime
        +is_revoked(): bool
    }

    class AuthService {
        +register_user(email, password): User
        +authenticate_user(email, password): User
        +logout(token): None
        +validate_token(token): bool
    }

    class ExtractorService {
        +get_indicator(symbol, indicator, days): dict
        +get_price_series(symbol, days): dict
        +get_quotes(symbols): dict
        -validate_inputs(): bool
    }

    class NLPExplainer {
        -templates: dict
        +generate_explanation(data, detail_level): dict
        +regenerate_explanation(data): dict
        -fill_template(template, data): string
    }

    class CoherenceValidator {
        +validate_coherence(indicator_data, text): tuple
        -check_rsi_terms(): bool
        -check_macd_terms(): bool
        -check_bollinger_terms(): bool
    }

    class ProfileService {
        +get_detail_level(user_id, indicator): string
        +build_learning_profile(user_id): dict
        +track_learning(user_id, concept): None
    }

    class WebController {
        +index(): html
        +api_instruments(): json
        +api_quotes(symbols): json
        +api_query(symbol, indicator): json
        +history(): html
        -run_query(symbol, indicator): dict
    }

    class Cache {
        -store: dict
        -ttl: int
        +get(key): any
        +set(key, value): None
        +clear(): None
    }

    class Exception {
        #message: string
    }

    class AuthError {
    }

    class ExtractionError {
    }

    %% Relaciones
    User "1" --> "0..*" QueryLog : generates
    User "1" --> "0..*" InstrumentVisit : visits

    WebController --> AuthService : uses
    WebController --> ExtractorService : uses
    WebController --> NLPExplainer : uses
    WebController --> ProfileService : uses
    WebController --> QueryLog : persists

    AuthService --> User : creates
    ExtractorService --> Cache : uses
    NLPExplainer --> CoherenceValidator : validates
    ProfileService --> QueryLog : reads
    ProfileService --> InstrumentVisit : reads

    Exception <|-- AuthError
    Exception <|-- ExtractionError
```

